## Author of Latest Modifications (`cmix-neif-3.1`)

* **Copyright (C) 2026 Oleksandr Dreval**
  * GitHub Profile: <https://github.com/OleksandrDreval>
  * Project Repository: <https://github.com/OleksandrDreval/cmix-neif-3.1>
  * Scope of copyright & GPL-3.0 section 5a modifications (November 2026):
    1. Stage-2 self-extracting stub `systrap` warm-up fix, stage-1 bootstrap
       context-mixer re-tuning, and single-pass forward `cm_compress_k` (`K = a.outn + 4`
       at `i == nd`) packer build (`1.51 GiB` peak RSS, `~39.0 s`, zero unpacker or
       decompressor executions) (`tools_src/packer/stub.c`, `tools_src/packer/boot_models.h`,
       `tools_src/packer/cm_core.h`, `tools_src/packer/pack_tool.c`,
       `tools_src/packer/build_packer.sh`, `build_and_construct_comp.sh`).
    2. Lossless `.c5` transformer weight container entropy-coding upgrades
       (Sign-Magnitude `ENC_INT4W`, per-canonical-name probability tables,
       16-bucket node-aware equal-weight density context `(w_mag + w_nd) >> 1` with `b` divisor `13312` (`M` prior `65536`),
       split-Dirichlet priors (`prr=6, pcc=8`, `dr1=384, dc1=12`, `dr2=64, dc2=20`, `ps_r=ps_c=192`),
       4-way integer probability mixing (`>> 5`) at each `ENC_INT4W` binary tree
       node (`wt = 23 - kW2d[node]`, `kW2d = {0, 4, 2, 2}`, `1/32` 3D, `8/32` `p_rc`) combining `p_tree`, 2D spatial context `p_2d` with RoPE parity `k & 1`,
       3D spatial context `p_3d`, and Bayesian row-column posterior `p_rc` on a
       stride-4 2-bit magnitude tree with 100 % Stream A `{0, ±2, ±4, ±7}` grid
       coverage, eliminating per-row `gbit` flags, inlining `last_zrow[1024]`, and
       shrinking `cname[16384]` to save `~792 KiB` in `ModelleId`; 4-way integer
       probability mixing (`11:6:4:11`, `sdr=256, sdc=256`) for `ENC_INT4W` signs
       combining `sign_int4w`, `sign_2d`, `sign_rc`, and continuous
       magnitude-weighted positive-dipole posterior `p_src` with full Lehmer
       Stream-B absorption `tailB = 0 B`; pre-snap 4-bit mantissa quantization
       (`(val + 8) & 0xFFF0`) and unconditional 4-bit `lo`-nibble shift-tree coding
       for all Stream A `ENC_BF16C` and `ENC_F32HC` tensors with order-1 `prev_hi`
       `CountNode` tree mixing and per-`ci` + row-$L_2$-energy-bucket /
       column-bucket + shared low-nibble shift-tree mixing; header byte-role mixing
       `cm_role[8 * 256]`, adaptive order-2/1/0 `cname` character tree mixing,
       per-`ci` `prev_z`-conditioned zero-row `zr_ctx[kNamenN * 2]` mixing;
       empirical QAT bimodal sparsity priors in `FrischInt4`, faster inter-block cross-tensor
       warm-start priors `CopyWarmCN` (shift `4`), two-stage `bfloat16` lo-byte adaptation
       shifts, `last_zrow` skipping of zero scales and dead KDA
       `key_convolution.weight` rows, and full-network continuous-target $\alpha$-rescaled
       (`\alpha_{\text{up}}=1.58, \alpha_{\text{dn}}=1.19, \alpha_{\text{qk}}=1.10, \alpha_{\text{v}}=1.12, \alpha_{\text{o}}=1.00, \alpha_{\text{g}}=1.19, \alpha_{\text{emb}}=1.06`) coupled `mlp.up`/`mlp.down`
       (`blocks.0..15` with full 16-block Lehmer re-permutation), KDA gate
       (`forget_gate_projection`, `output_gate_projection`),
       `attention.{query,key,value,output}_projection` (`blocks.0..15`), and
       `embedding.*` / `value_embeddings.0..3` / `prior_embedding`
       multi-candidate `{0, ±2, ±4, ±7}` Lagrangian Rate-Distortion QAT snapping
       `qat-snap` with feature-Gram $G_{\text{up}}$ coordinate descent and
       closed-form analytical $\text{ReLU}^2$/linear cross-covariance compensation)
       and re-encoded `2,535,202 B` container
       `weights-poc8m_w2048_tf2t3_pruned_v5k_np2.c5` (`src/tf1/`,
       `src/transformer.h`, `training/tf/3_train/export/np2/tf1_np_codec.cpp`).
    3. `BITLSTM` slot-1 3-bit mantissa rounding, single-byte `(e_code << 4) | s`
       `kBlobW[24669]` packing (`-24,489 B` `.rodata`, `-49.8 %`) with 90-byte
       exception tail (`kSlotExcOff[3] = {0, 4, 55}`), active-cell `H = kSlotH[slot]`
       (`H = 16` via `Dot16Preloaded` for slot 0, `H = 32` via `Dot32Preloaded`
       for slots 1 and 2) 100 % IEEE-754 bit-exact frozen AVX2 inference fast-path
       with transposed non-FMA `hidP` projection and pruning of 39 dead training
       fields from `struct Head` (`src/bit_head_weights.h`, `src/bit_head.cpp`),
       plus `tf1` SIMD kernel deduplication, zero-block fast-paths, and unified
       sparse GEMV dispatch (`src/tf1/opt/model_opt.cpp`, `src/tf1/opt/qmat_dense.cpp`,
       `src/tf1/opt/qmat_sparse.cpp`, shrinking `.decomp_bin` to `183,868 B`), AVX2
       column-scaling in `mixer_precond.cpp`, dead-code pruning (`sse.cpp`,
       `glibc_compat.cpp`, `ppmd_page.{h,cpp}`), and `COLD_SIZE_ATTR` layout.
    4. ~2.92x peak RAM reduction across the `PPMd` page pool (`zonen_textrahmen`
       `4 MiB` rounding fix, removal of phantom `+2.12 GiB` `ppmd_page::raum`
       pre-accounting, demand-paged `memfd`), single-mapping demand-paged
       `SEMCACHE` (`MAP_NORESERVE` + `FreeFxcmRest` `munmap` with exact
       `kNLog = 24, kB = 18` SimHash geometry), `word_label` 69 MiB leak fix in
       `FreeFxcmRest()` and `PAGE_REGISTRY_ADD` dangling-pointer removal,
       decompressor/postprocessor memory-safety & `~161 MiB` peak heap reduction
       (`article_reorder.h`, `komm_transform.h`, `page_form.h`,
       `phda9_preprocess.h`, `cmtidx_transform.h`, `census_transform.h`,
       `preprocessor.cpp`, `runner.cpp`, `misc.h` vectorized `memchr`/`memmem`
       I/O), and 4 KiB demand-paged `arena` / `HugeBuf` allocators, plus 4-row
       AVX2 unrolling in `SemDotPm1` (`src/models/ppmd*.{h,cpp}`,
       `src/semantic_cache.h`, `src/predictor.cpp`, `src/word_label.cpp`,
       `src/runner.cpp`, `src/arena_alloc.h`, `src/tf1/opt/arena_build.cpp`).
    5. Compiler warning cleanups and PGO diagnostic flags across `src/` and
       `makefile`, plus analytical/benchmark documentation
       (`en-optimization_report_it_1.md`..`en-optimization_report_it_8.md`,
       `uk-optimization_report_it_1.md`..`uk-optimization_report_it_8.md`,
       `CHANGES.md`, `NOTICE.md`, `README.md`, `training/`).

No copyright claim is made by Oleksandr Dreval over inherited upstream code;
his copyright claim covers the `cmix-neif-3.1` modifications and reports only,
licensed under `GPL-3.0-only`.

